Question: "A game of Plinko is played by dropping a ball at the top-middle of a set of pegs. Each time the ball hits a peg, it has a $\frac{1}{2}$ probability of deflecting either to the left or to the right. What is the probability that the ball lands in the middle slot as shown in the diagram (the red line)? [asy]
size(3inch, 2.25inch);
for (int i = 0; i < 8; i += 2) {

draw(circle((0, i + 1), 0.1));

draw(circle((2, i + 1), 0.1));

draw(circle((4, i + 1), 0.1));

draw(circle((6, i + 1), 0.1));

draw(circle((8, i + 1), 0.1));

draw(circle((10, i + 1), 0.1));

draw(circle((12, i + 1), 0.1));

draw(circle((14, i + 1), 0.1));

draw(circle((16, i + 1), 0.1));

draw(circle((1, i), 0.1));

draw(circle((3, i), 0.1));

draw(circle((5, i), 0.1));

draw(circle((7, i), 0.1));

draw(circle((9, i), 0.1));

draw(circle((11, i), 0.1));

draw(circle((13, i), 0.1));

draw(circle((15, i), 0.1));
}

pen target = red + linewidth(2);

draw((-0.8, -1)--(0.8, -1));
draw((1.2, -1)--(2.8, -1));
draw((3.2, -1)--(4.8, -1));
draw((5.2, -1)--(6.8, -1));
draw((7.2, -1)--(8.8, -1), target);
draw((9.2, -1)--(10.8, -1));
draw((11.2, -1)--(12.8, -1));
draw((13.2, -1)--(14.8, -1));
draw((15.2, -1)--(16.8, -1));

pen tube = black + linewidth(2);
draw((7.2, 9)--(7.2, 7.8)--(8.8, 7.8)--(8.8, 9), tube);

filldraw(Circle((8, 8.5), 0.6), blue);
[/asy]"
Solution: "For the ball to end up back in the center, the ball must deflect left 4 of the 8 times, and right the other 4 times. There are $\binom{8}{4}$ ways to pick which 4 of the rows to deflect the ball left and then the other 4 to deflect it right.  Each deflection is to the left with probability $\frac12$ and to the right with probability $\frac12$, so each possible path to the bottom occurs with probability $\left(\dfrac{1}{2}\right)^{\!8}$.  Thus, the probability that 4 out of 8 deflections go left and the ball goes in the middle is \[\binom{8}{4}\frac{1}{2^8}=\boxed{\frac{35}{128}}.\]"

